SUMMARY:Deadline: Nieman Fellowships at Harvard\, Class of 2028
DESCRIPTION:The Nieman Foundation brings around two dozen journalists to Ha
 rvard each year for two semesters of study\, reflection and community\, on
 e of the oldest and best-known midcareer journalism fellowships in the wor
 ld.\n\nOrganisation: Nieman Foundation for Journalism at Harvard\nLocation
 : Cambridge\, Massachusetts\, USA (residential academic year at Harvard)\n
 Award: USD 87\,500 stipend paid over the nine-month academic year (2026-27
  figure)\, plus additional allowances for housing\, childcare and health i
 nsurance. Fellows audit courses across Harvard and participate in Nieman s
 eminars\, master classes and workshops. No application fee.\nDuration: Two
  semesters in residence at Harvard\, academic year 2027-28\n\nMore: https:
 //nieman.harvard.edu/fellowships/how-to-apply/?utm_source=artificialnouvea
 ugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://nieman.harvard.edu/fellowships/how-to-apply/?utm_source=artific
 ialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Cambridge\, Massachusetts\, USA (residential academic year at Harv
 ard)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:open-notebook-early-career-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T150308Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261031
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:Deadline: The Open Notebook Early-Career Fellowship 2027 (remote)
DESCRIPTION:The Open Notebook's paid fellowship for early-career science jo
 urnalists is open for its 2027 round. Fellows spend twelve months working 
 part-time and remotely with a personal mentor\, reporting and writing arti
 cles about the craft of science journalism that are published at The Open 
 Notebook\, one of the field's central craft resources.\n\nOrganisation: Th
 e Open Notebook\nLocation: Remote\, worldwide. Application materials in En
 glish\; international applicants welcome.\nAward: USD 6\,600 stipend over 
 the twelve-month part-time fellowship\, plus one-on-one mentoring from an 
 experienced science journalist and published clips at The Open Notebook. N
 o application fee.\nDuration: 12 months part-time\, starting 9 February 20
 27.\n\nMore: https://www.theopennotebook.com/early-career-fellowship-progr
 am/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.theopennotebook.com/early-career-fellowship-program/?utm_so
 urce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote\, worldwide. Application materials in English\; internation
 al applicants welcome.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
