DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261103
SUMMARY:Deadline: Inciter Art (Fractured Atlas): quarterly open call for es
 says\, 'tending to the hearth' (USD 750 stipend)
DESCRIPTION:Inciter Art\, the Fractured Atlas blog\, runs themed quarterly 
 open calls for short essays by artists and arts workers\, and this season'
 s theme is 'tending to the hearth': generosity\, solidarity and collective
  investment in the invisible infrastructure behind creative work.\n\nOrgan
 isation: Fractured Atlas (Inciter Art)\nLocation: Remote (online publicati
 on)\; payment via W-9\, so US-based writers in practice.\nAward: USD 750 s
 tipend per selected writer\, paid by ACH deposit or check once the first d
 raft is finished (a W-9 form is required). No submission fee.\nDuration: A
 bout six weeks after selection: four weeks for a first draft\, one week fo
 r the final draft.\n\nMore: https://fracturedatlas.notion.site/3cf23f9f3dc
 880bd91dbfbe1a70df620?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=ref
 erral
URL:https://fracturedatlas.notion.site/3cf23f9f3dc880bd91dbfbe1a70df620?utm
 _source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote (online publication)\; payment via W-9\, so US-based writer
 s in practice.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:in-development-asterisk-ai-developing-countries-essay-contest-2026@arti
 ficialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T150308Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261231
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270101
SUMMARY:Deadline: In Development x Asterisk Essay Contest: How Will AI Affe
 ct Developing Countries? (USD 10\,000 top prize)
DESCRIPTION:An essay contest run by the development-economics publication I
 n Development and Asterisk Magazine on how transformative AI will affect l
 ow- and middle-income countries\, and how those countries might respond.\n
 \nOrganisation: In Development and Asterisk Magazine\, with a special priz
 e from the African Tech Futures Lab\nLocation: Worldwide\, online submissi
 on. Authors based in low- and middle-income countries particularly encoura
 ged.\nAward: Winner USD 10\,000 plus publication in Asterisk (print and on
 line) and In Development\; two runners-up USD 5\,000 each plus publication
  in Asterisk (online) and In Development\; two honourable mentions USD 2\,
 000 each. Separate African Tech Futures Lab prize of USD 2\,500 for the be
 st essay by an African national\, combinable with the main prizes. No entr
 y fee stated.\n\nMore: https://indevelopmentmag.substack.com/p/how-will-ai
 -affect-developing-countries?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
URL:https://indevelopmentmag.substack.com/p/how-will-ai-affect-developing-c
 ountries?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Worldwide\, online submission. Authors based in low- and middle-in
 come countries particularly encouraged.
